# Diagnosing bugs

**Build a tight, red-capable feedback loop first** — a single command that reproduces the user's
exact symptom and goes green when fixed. That is 90% of the work; don't theorize before it exists.
Then: reproduce + minimise → generate 3–5 falsifiable ranked hypotheses → instrument one variable
at a time (tag debug logs) → fix with a regression test → clean up and note the root cause.
